        <groundspeak:log id="676636115">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2827702">bunnyberm</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP379 Bragg Creek

I sort of know how this works, and I see TTOS logged his find and my photo on this page, so I'll log mine as well, and email OFTH with the info. :-)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="675752434">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="721008">TheTowerOfSong</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP379 Bragg Creek&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headed out today for a little walk in West Bragg and FINALLY stopped for this cap! Will try to get in a few others before that fateful day but I will not dwell on the 'Groundspeak Logic'.

A very easy cap to find with little walking and searching required!  Not your typical cap in the wilds, that is for sure!

Found with BunnyBerm and this is his FIRST cap to log! Proud to be with him for it.

Will send the requisite info off to the OFTH (thank you again for keeping this one going for so very long) and tip of the hat to all you cappers out there!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="666385119">
